.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-validate\-references <string>\fR
Whether Emporix checks that the items that references in the body name exist (false without it, although its reference says true), requesting custom.<type>_read where it is true: true or false.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx custom\-entities instances bulk\-update"
Upsert instances of a custom entity type in bulk.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx custom\-entities instances bulk\-update CUSTOM_ENTITY_ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Replaces the instances of the custom entity type CUSTOM_ENTITY_ID in \fB\-\-file\fR, a JSON array of instances, each with its id and as update takes it, or creates those that do not exist (an upsert). CUSTOM_ENTITY_ID is the ID that \fBepx custom\-entities list\fR shows.
.PP
With \fB\-\-validate\-references\fR true, Emporix checks the items that the references of each instance name with epx\(aqs token, which reads the instances of CUSTOM_ENTITY_ID alone: an instance with a reference to an item that does not exist fails with 500 Internal Server Error (nothing is created), as one with a reference to an instance of another custom entity type is expected to, and one with a reference to another kind of item, such as a product, may.
